<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?><!--
  The launcher foreground: one bold wave.

  It replaces a plain play triangle, which said "a media app" and nothing more. The wave is the
  same motif as the docked player's `LinearWavyProgressIndicator` — the most recognisable thing on
  Wanda's own surface and a Material 3 Expressive signature — so the icon says which player this is
  rather than merely that it plays something.

  Geometry is kept well inside the mask. Adaptive launchers can crop to a circle of roughly 66dp
  across the 108dp canvas: the wave spans x 30..78 and peaks at y 42 and 66, so with a 10dp stroke
  its furthest point sits about 29dp from centre — clear of the 33dp radius on any mask shape.

  The amplitude is deliberately generous. A shallower wave was tried first and read as timid at
  launcher size, which is the opposite of what this style is for.

  Four cubic half-cycles rather than a traced outline, so the curve stays smooth at every density
  and the stroke width is a single number to tune.
-->
<vector xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    android:width="108dp"
    android:height="108dp"
    android:viewportWidth="108"
    android:viewportHeight="108">

    <path
        android:strokeColor="#FFFFFF"
        android:strokeWidth="10"
        android:strokeLineCap="round"
        android:strokeLineJoin="round"
        android:fillColor="@android:color/transparent"
        android:pathData="M30,54 C34,38 38,38 42,54 C46,70 50,70 54,54 C58,38 62,38 66,54 C70,70 74,70 78,54" />
</vector>
